00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:58.190
Their fight is going to be awesome though,
mostly because they're both such good fighters.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:02.300
So let's jump in the ring and try to figure
out who the best fighter in a song of ice

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:05.369
and fire is. Number 10 - Young Ned Stark

00:01:05.369 --> 00:01:10.890
I'm mostly talking about him during Robert's
Rebellion. He wasn't big on Tourneys or Jousting.

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:16.150
Just traditional warfare and swordplay. In
battle he primarily used his two handed valyrian

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:20.750
greatsword Ice. I thought he deserved this
spot on the list because he fought and killed

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:25.290
Ser Arthur Dayne the Sword of the Morning
during the rebellion. Dayne was a member of

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:30.100
King Aerys Kingsguard and Ned led the charge
during the sack of King's Landing. It was

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:34.619
right after that he found Jaime Lannister
killing King Aerys, he was like the first

00:01:34.619 --> 00:01:36.200
person on the scene.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:40.500
Killing Arthur Dayne was a huge deal because
he was supposed to be one of the best fighters

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:47.399
in the world. He just like Ned Stark, had
a two handed Greatsword called Dawn, it wasn't

00:01:47.399 --> 00:01:53.619
valyrian steel, but it was supposedly forged
from a fallen star and was just as sharp as

00:01:53.619 --> 00:02:00.619
valyrian steel. So imagine Ned Stark and Arthur
Dayne swinging two giant indestructible greatswords

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:06.369
at each other. Like two giant lightsabers.
There would have been crazy sparks flying

00:02:06.369 --> 00:02:10.050
off their impacts.

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:13.690
We know what happened to Ned Stark's blade,
it was melted down by Twyin Lannister into

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:19.120
Oathkeeper and Widow's Wail. After Ned Stark
killed Arthur Dayne he rode to Starfall to

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:22.790
give Dawn to Ashara Dayne, the sister of Arthur
Dayne.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:26.569
That's where the rumor about Ashara Dayne
being Jon Snow's mother comes from. I don't

00:02:26.569 --> 00:02:27.720
believe it, but the rumor exists.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.360
Number 9 - The Knight Of The Laughing Tree

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:34.500
This is one of the most mysterious fighters
in the books. Whenever Jaime Lannister had

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:39.510
his induction ceremony to the Kingsgaurd,
King Aerys threw a Tournament at Harrenhal.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:45.510
A teenage Howland Reed got bullied by the
squires of house Haigh, House Blount and House

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:48.269
Frey.
Howland Reed just for reference is the father

00:02:48.269 --> 00:02:54.010
of Jojen and Meera Reed, the ones helping
Bran. But this all happened way before they

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:59.920
were born. Because the Reed's are Stark Bannerman,
Lyanna Stark rushed up and beat off the squires

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:01.280
with a sword.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.379
Later as a way to defend Reed's honor, a really
small mystery knight with mismatched patchwork

00:03:04.379 --> 00:03:10.340
armor showed up in the jousting tournament
and defeated the Knights from all those squires

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:10.900
houses.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:14.250
The reason the mystery knight was called the
knight of the laughing tree was because the

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:17.230
shield had a white weirwood tree on it with
a laughing red face. Supposedly the person

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.110
had a booming voice when they shouted through
their helm.

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:23.769
Because defeating all those knights was a
huge deal, Robert Baratheon who was super

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:30.769
competitive and King Aery's demanded that
they unmask the mystery knight to find out

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:34.190
who it was. Aerys sent Rhaegar Targaryen to
find them, but when the person ran off all

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:37.290
he came back with was the knight's shield
with the laughing tree on it.

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:42.260
The best theory's I've seen as to who it was
is Lyanna Stark, it makes sense that she would

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:47.140
be trained to fight. Ned Stark even said that
Arya, who's becoming a pretty badass fighter

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:51.500
herself, resembles Lyanna. So my theory is
that Rhaegar found out she was the mystery

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:56.310
knight, fell in love and just never told his
father king Aerys. Cut to them running away

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:59.349
together, then Robert's Rebellion.

00:03:59.349 --> 00:04:06.349
So I think the R + L equals J theory flows
from the Knight of the Laughing Tree. If you

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:13.390
want to read about Laughing Tree in the books
it's in the Bran 2 chapter of Book 3.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:15.819
Number 8 - Brienne of Tarth

00:04:15.819 --> 00:04:19.560
She's not quite as big as the Mountain, but
she's bigger and faster than most of the other

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:23.250
knights that are still alive on the show.
She doesn't have the experience of someone

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:28.960
like Areo Hotah or Barristan Selmy. But she
was able to beat the crap out of a weakened

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:33.479
Jaime Lannister. Who is also one of the best
fighters in Westeros, before he lost his hand.

00:04:33.479 --> 00:04:40.000
I could also cite Brienne smashing the hell
out of Loras Tyrell during the war of the

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:47.000
five kings. Usually the biggest fighters on
the show only get beaten when they make mistakes

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:52.759
or fight someone quicker. And Brienne is big
and Quick.

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:57.940
Her weakness, like most knights is her hubris.
It's pretty easy to get under her skin as

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:02.280
seen during the Purple Wedding when Cersei
Lannister went all Mean Girls on her. Before

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:06.560
they became really close, Jaime also got under
her skin quite a bit.

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:09.979
I'd really like to see Brienne fight Obara
Sand just because they're good approximations

00:05:09.979 --> 00:05:12.810
of each other. I think they would be pretty
evenly matched. Obara is a little smaller,

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:17.310
but she wields a pike like her father Oberyn
Martell.

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:20.860
Number 7 - Jaime Lannister When He Still Had
Two Hands

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:25.380
Jaime earned his knighthood by killing the
Smiling Knight when Arthur Dayne and a bunch

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:30.060
of King Aery's men were trying to rescue someone
from a big group of outlaws called the Kingswood

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:34.259
Brotherhood. Think of them as being like the
previous iteration of the Brave Companions

00:05:34.259 --> 00:05:36.110
or Locke's Group on the show.

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:41.960
The Smiling Knight was like the previous generations
version of The Mountain. Completely psychotic

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:47.800
and very dangerous. When Arthur Dayne found
Jaime had killed him, he knighted him immediately

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:49.259
on the battlefield.

00:05:49.259 --> 00:05:54.120
Funny side story. After all this happened
Jaime learned Twyin intended to marry him

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:59.800
to Lysa Tulley. Yes, that Lysa Tulley that
took a trip through the Moon Door. So Cersei

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:05.090
suggested he join the Kingsguard to escape
and be close to her. Cersei is pretty selfish,

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:12.090
but in this case I'd say she helped Jaime
sidestep that land mine.

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:16.090
Number 6 - Greatjon Umber

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:20.419
He's the head of House Umber, they're Stark
Bannermen. He was at the Red Wedding and was

00:06:20.419 --> 00:06:26.289
taken captive by the Frey's but he's still
alive. The reason he's on this list is because

00:06:26.289 --> 00:06:31.490
he's one of the only people Jaime Lannister
thinks could beat him in a fight. This is

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:37.880
pre-accident Jaime. Greatjon is huge like
the Mountain but he's not psychotic. So he's

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:40.330
really only dangerous if challenged in battle.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:45.360
Because he's so huge he wields a two handed
greatsword that's even bigger than Ned Starks.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:51.050
His isn't valyrian steel, but Robb Stark called
it the ugliest blade he'd ever seen. I think

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:52.680
he meant ugly in the sense it was fearsome.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:54.650
Number 5 - The Mountain

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:59.479
We just met the new actor playing the Mountain
in episode 7. It's the third person to play

00:06:59.479 --> 00:07:05.319
the role. He's supposed to be about 8 feet
tall and weigh about 420 pounds. That makes

00:07:05.319 --> 00:07:10.940
him the largest human person in the world.
That we know about. If Strong Belwas were

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:13.669
on the show I still think the Mountain would
be bigger.

00:07:13.669 --> 00:07:18.789
His armor is crazy. It's so heavy that he's
the only one that can wear it and still move.

00:07:18.789 --> 00:07:24.389
It's the thickest plate of any armor in westeros
underneath which he has a layer of chainmail

00:07:24.389 --> 00:07:30.090
and boiled leather.
He is a big dumb animal compared to other

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:34.919
more scholarly characters, but he has excellent
warrior instincts and he's very quick. So

00:07:34.919 --> 00:07:41.009
add excellent fighter to fortress like armor
and you get an almost invincible fighter.

00:07:41.009 --> 00:07:44.530
Supposedly he does have constant persistent
headaches that are either related to his gigantism

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:48.550
or a severe blow to the head during a random
tournament. There's a theory that this is

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:52.949
part of the reason why he's so psychotic,
he suffered a brain injury that just went

00:07:52.949 --> 00:07:53.190
untreated.

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:58.210
I have a really huge theory about The Mountain
as it relates to Robert Strong who we haven't

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:03.000
met yet. So I'm going to wait until Season
5 to talk about that. But if you've read the

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:09.039
books and want to discuss theories, just use
the spoiler tag and hit enter four or five

00:08:09.039 --> 00:08:10.220
times before writing stuff.

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:11.849
Number 4 - Oberyn Martell

00:08:11.849 --> 00:08:17.099
Yes, I totally think Oberyn Martell is a better
fighter than The Mountain. Please don't go

00:08:17.099 --> 00:08:23.949
crazy with spoilers. The reason I think Oberyn
is better is because he's way way quicker,

00:08:23.949 --> 00:08:30.949
he uses a pike in battle and he has expert
knowledge of poisons.

00:08:31.479 --> 00:08:37.010
So all of those things just provide him with
the tools for fighting really big people like

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:41.339
The Mountain.

00:08:41.339 --> 00:08:43.539
Number 3 - Areo Hotah

00:08:43.539 --> 00:08:48.430
He's like the Barristan Selmy of the Martell
family in Dorne. He protects Oberyn's Brother

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:54.459
Prince Doran. He wields a long axe that's
about six feet.

00:08:54.459 --> 00:08:59.660
He was trained by the Bearded Priests of Norvos
in the free cities. The common saying is that

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:03.709
people of that order are wedded to their Axes.
They're like a really prominent fighting school

00:09:03.709 --> 00:09:06.380
that trains people to fight and protect.

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:12.370
Just like Barristan Selmy he's very formal
and utterly loyal to Prince Doran. In Selmy's

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:13.670
case it's Daenerys.

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:16.360
Number 2 - Barristan Selmy

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:21.470
He trained with Ser Duncan the Tall and Prince
Duncan the small from the Dunk and Egg stories.

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:25.480
And ended up becoming one of the greatest
knights in the history of Westeros. Early

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:29.950
in his life he earned most of his respect
during the War of the Ninepenny Kings after

00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:32.209
he killed one of the Blackfyre pretenders.

00:09:32.209 --> 00:09:37.730
He was also at the famous Tourney of Harrenhal
where the Knight of the Laughing Tree was.

00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:42.350
He got unhorsed by Rhaegar Targaryen who ended
up winning the tournament. But I still consider

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:46.570
Barristan Selmy to be a better fighter.
It's like Ned Stark told Jaime Lannister,

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:51.760
play fighting in tournaments is one thing.
Fighting on the battlefield is another.

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:56.980
Number 1 - Young Robert Baratheon

00:09:56.980 --> 00:10:01.180
Even though on the show we only see him after
his better years are over. When he was young

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:06.950
he was like the Hollywood Leading Man of Westeros.
Not super bright, but very charismatic and

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:08.620
an amazing fighter.

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:12.540
If they had holodecks in Game of Thrones,
Robert would have just spent his entire life

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:16.820
in a never ending battle. That's why he peaked
during the rebellion. Because he was at the

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:22.120
height of his physical prowess and was so
good at making war.

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:26.920
Since this list should have been like a top
50 fighters here's a couple of people I think

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:29.959
deserve to be mentioned, but I couldn't find
a spot for them on the list.

00:10:29.959 --> 00:10:36.959
Strong Belwas, The Hound, Syrio Forel, Arthur
Dayne, Ser Duncan The Tall, Obara Sand and

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:44.510
Daeron the Young Dragon. There's a ton of
other people that we just don't know a ton

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:47.779
about. So I'm hoping the new books give us
some more context.

00:10:47.779 --> 00:10:51.950
Now it's your turn, let me know who you think
is the best fighter on Game Of Thrones, either

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:55.440
